Once the found flag of the X-fold is 1, a point lies in the presentation image of the running code if and only if it lies in the image of some non-junk half-step atom below that stage.

The argument is induction on the stage. Zero is impossible because the flag starts at 0. At a successor the step is unfolded. If the current atom is non-junk and the previous flag is 0, the new code is that atom, so membership is the witness at the new index, while an earlier witness would already have raised the previous flag. If the previous flag is 1, the running image and the new atom are genuine neighbourhoods, so their union has a presentation code, and the union-index specification together with the inductive hypothesis splits membership into an earlier witness or the new atom. If the current atom is junk, the accumulator is unchanged, the inductive hypothesis extends the bound, and the new index is impossible.
